From 48071efd4172c225ba80f0aae340ce2209e2a658 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:52:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(kernel): divide a runaway strip face over its
 boundary nodes

solidcore-tess plans a long thin strip (a thread flank) isotropically:
the four-turn fixture got 391338 facets after the replan at half the
chord. The seam can only pick the chord of the planner.

The seam now gives a face with a runaway count a second division: the
Delaunay fill of its boundary loop over its shared edge nodes, with no
node inside (ear clipping and Lawson flips, mesh_redivide_fill). It keeps
that division only when mesh_deviation::measure_within proves it inside
the tolerance; if not, the face keeps the planner's triangles. The
measure of the whole plan runs after it as before.

The thread flank meshes in 1150 facets, measured 3.8e-3 mm at 5e-3 mm.
The known-fail marker of the pin is removed.

Fixes #2844

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
